{"representative_mt_stained_slides": "Representative MT-stained slides are examples of tissue samples that have been stained using the Masson's Trichrome (MT) method, which is commonly used to highlight fibrous tissue in histological samples."},
{"representative_mt_stained_slides__show__ai_generated_overlays_highlighting_regions_of_fibrosis_present_on_biopsies": "The predicate \"show\" indicates that the MT-stained slides are being used to visually display or demonstrate something, in this case, the AI-generated overlays."},
{"ai_generated_overlays_highlighting_regions_of_fibrosis_present_on_biopsies": "AI-generated overlays highlighting regions of fibrosis present on biopsies are digital annotations created by an artificial intelligence system to mark areas of fibrotic tissue on the MT-stained slides, aiding in the qualitative assessment of fibrosis stages."},
{"representative_cases__correspond_to__mash_crn_fibrosis_stages_f1_total_n_159_f2_total_n_146_f3_total_n_278_and_f4_total_n_23": "The phrase \"correspond to\" indicates a direct relationship where the representative cases are matched or aligned with specific MASH CRN fibrosis stages, as determined by both pathologist consensus scoring and AI in the test set."},
{"mash_crn_fibrosis_stages_f1_total_n_159_f2_total_n_146_f3_total_n_278_and_f4_total_n_23": "MASH CRN fibrosis stages F1, F2, F3, and F4 are specific categories used to classify the severity of fibrosis in MASH disease. These stages are represented by a total of 159 cases for F1, 146 cases for F2, 278 cases for F3, and 23 cases for F4, as identified by both pathologists and AI."},
{"ai_generated_overlays": "AI-generated overlays are visual annotations created by artificial intelligence algorithms to highlight specific features or regions within medical images, such as histopathologic slides."},
