{"proportionate_area_measurements": "Proportionate area measurements refer to the method of quantifying the extent of specific features within histological slides by measuring the area they occupy relative to the total area of the slide.|Here is another description: Proportionate area measurements refer to the specific method of quantifying the extent of various histological features within tissue samples, such as the degree of steatosis, ballooning, inflammation, and fibrosis observed in H&E and MT stained slides."},
