{"predictions__were_derived_from__cnn_image_segmentation_algorithms": "The phrase \"were derived from\" indicates the source or method used to obtain the predictions. In this context, it signifies that the predictions were generated or obtained using a specific technology or algorithm."},
{"cnn_image_segmentation_algorithms": "CNN image segmentation algorithms are advanced machine learning techniques used for analyzing and segmenting images. In this context, they are employed to produce the spatially resolved predictions that serve as inputs for training GNNs."},
{"pathologists": "Pathologists are medical professionals who specialize in diagnosing diseases by examining tissues and cells under a microscope. They provide detailed annotations and assessments on whole slide images (WSIs) to aid in the development and training of AI and machine learning models for medical imaging, including the grading of liver disease severity and the evaluation of histologic features in liver biopsies.|Here is another description: Pathologists are medical doctors who specialize in the diagnosis of diseases by examining tissues and cells under a microscope. They play a crucial role in providing accurate diagnoses that inform patient treatment plans.|Here is another description: Pathologists are medical professionals specialized in the diagnosis of diseases by examining tissues and cells under a microscope. They play a crucial role in providing accurate diagnoses that inform patient treatment plans."},
{"pathologists__provided__slide_level_mash_crn_grades_stages": "The predicate \"provided\" indicates that the pathologists supplied or furnished the necessary data or information. In this case, they offered slide-level MASH CRN grades/stages, which are critical for training machine learning models.|Here is another description: The action \"provided\" indicates that the pathologists supplied or delivered something\u2014in this case, slide-level MASH CRN grades/stages\u2014as part of their evaluation process."},
{"slide_level_mash_crn_grades_stages": "Slide-level MASH CRN grades/stages are detailed assessments by pathologists of liver tissue slides, evaluating histologic features like steatosis, ballooning, lobular inflammation, and fibrosis. These grades/stages, based on MASH CRN criteria, are essential for diagnosing and staging liver diseases such as MASH."},
{"gnns__were_trained_using__spatially_resolved_predictions_and_slide_level_mash_crn_grades_stages": "The phrase \"were trained using\" indicates the process by which the GNNs were equipped with the ability to make predictions. This involved utilizing specific types of data as inputs during the training phase to learn patterns and relationships."},
{"spatially_resolved_predictions_and_slide_level_mash_crn_grades_stages": "Spatially resolved predictions refer to detailed, location-specific predictions made by CNN image segmentation algorithms, which break down an image into segments and analyze each part. Slide-level MASH CRN grades/stages are comprehensive assessments provided by pathologists that evaluate the overall condition of a tissue sample on a slide, according to the MASH CRN grading system."},
{"nature_medicine__specific_page__2916": "The specific_page predicate indicates the exact page number within the journal where a particular article or section can be found. This helps readers quickly locate the content they are interested in."},
