{"\u03ba_statistics": "\u03ba statistics refer to a measure of agreement or reliability, often used in medical and statistical contexts to evaluate the consistency of ratings or classifications made by different observers or methods.|Here is another description: \u03ba statistics refer to a measure of agreement or reliability in the context of evaluating the performance of AIM-MASH grades/stages versus a consensus of expert pathologists. These statistics are crucial for comparing the consistency and accuracy of different assessments.|Here is another description: \u03ba statistics, also known as Cohen's kappa, is a statistical measure used to assess the level of agreement between two raters when the ratings are categorical. In this context, \u03ba statistics were used to quantify the concordance between the AI's assessments and the consensus determinations made by expert pathologists."},
