{"loomba_r_et_al__reviewed__fda_and_ema_guidance_on_drug_development_and_endpoints_in_nonalcoholic_steatohepatitis": "The predicate'reviewed' indicates that the subject, Loomba, R. et al., conducted a critical examination and analysis of existing guidelines or documents. In this context, it means that the researchers assessed and compared the FDA and EMA guidance on drug development and endpoints in nonalcoholic steatohepatitis."},
{"fda_and_ema_guidance_on_drug_development_and_endpoints_in_nonalcoholic_steatohepatitis": "The object 'FDA and EMA guidance on drug development and endpoints in nonalcoholic steatohepatitis' refers to the official recommendations and standards set by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) and the European Medicines Agency (EMA) for the development of drugs aimed at treating nonalcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH). These guidelines outline the criteria and endpoints that clinical trials must meet to demonstrate the efficacy and safety of new drugs for NASH."},
{"bedossa_p_flip_pathology_consortium": "Bedossa, P. & FLIP Pathology Consortium refers to a collaborative group led by Pierre Bedossa, focused on the pathology and evaluation of liver diseases, particularly nonalcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD).|Here is another description: Bedossa, P. & FLIP Pathology Consortium is a group of researchers led by Pierre Bedossa, focused on the study and evaluation of liver diseases, particularly nonalcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD)."},
