{"simtuzumab_for_primary_sclerosing_cholangitis": "Simtuzumab for primary sclerosing cholangitis refers to the use of Simtuzumab, a monoclonal antibody, in the treatment of primary sclerosing cholangitis (PSC), a chronic liver disease characterized by inflammation and fibrosis of the bile ducts. The study aimed to assess the efficacy and safety of Simtuzumab in managing PSC."},
{"hirschfield_g_m_et_al": "Hirschfield, G. M. et al. refers to a group of researchers led by G. M. Hirschfield who conducted a study on the efficacy and safety of seladelpar in patients with primary biliary cholangitis.|Here is another description: Hirschfield, G. M. et al. refers to a group of researchers led by G. M. Hirschfield who conducted a study. This group is recognized for their collaborative work in the field of hepatology, particularly in clinical trials involving liver diseases."},
