{"artificial_intelligence_based_measurement_of_nash_histology_aim_nash_recapitulates_primary_results_from_phase_3_study_of_resmetirom_for_treatment_of_nash_mash": "Artificial intelligence-based measurement of NASH histology (AIM-NASH) recapitulates primary results from phase 3 study of resmetirom for treatment of NASH/MASH refers to a method using artificial intelligence to measure the histology of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH), which was found to replicate the primary results from a phase 3 clinical study of resmetirom, a drug used for the treatment of NASH."},
{"cable_e_e_et_al": "Cable, E. E. et al. refers to a group of researchers led by E. E. Cable who conducted a study on non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH) using advanced technology."},
{"cable_e_e_et_al__assessed__nash_pathologies_in_152_baseline_h_e_slides_from_a_phase_2_trial_using_the_pathai_machine_learning_algorithm": "The predicate \"assessed\" indicates that the researchers evaluated or analyzed something using a specific method or tool."},
{"nash_pathologies_in_152_baseline_h_e_slides_from_a_phase_2_trial_using_the_pathai_machine_learning_algorithm": "NASH pathologies in 152 baseline H&E slides from a phase 2 trial using the PathAI machine learning algorithm refers to the evaluation of liver tissue samples stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) from a clinical trial, using an artificial intelligence-based machine learning algorithm developed by PathAI to identify and quantify NASH-related features."},
{"shevell_d_e_et_al": "Shevell, D. E. et al. refers to a group of researchers led by D. E. Shevell who conducted a study comparing different methods for scoring liver biopsies."},
{"shevell_d_e_et_al__compared__manual_vs_machine_learning_approaches_to_liver_biopsy_scoring_for_nash_and_fibrosis": "The predicate \"compared\" indicates that the researchers evaluated and contrasted two different approaches\u2014manual and machine learning\u2014for scoring liver biopsies in the context of NASH and fibrosis."},
{"manual_vs_machine_learning_approaches_to_liver_biopsy_scoring_for_nash_and_fibrosis": "The object \"manual vs. machine learning approaches to liver biopsy scoring for NASH and fibrosis\" describes the two methods under comparison: traditional manual scoring by pathologists and automated scoring using machine learning algorithms, both aimed at assessing the severity of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH) and fibrosis in liver biopsies."},
{"harrison_s_et_al": "Harrison, S. et al. refers to a group of researchers led by Dr. Stephen Harrison, who are involved in studies related to non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH) and its treatment."},
