{"hematoxylin_and_eosin": "Hematoxylin and eosin are two dyes used together in a common staining technique in histology to differentiate between various types of tissues and cells under a microscope. Hematoxylin stains cell nuclei blue, while eosin stains the cytoplasm and other extracellular components pink."},
