{"crn_fibrosis_scores": "CRN fibrosis scores refer to a system used to evaluate the degree of liver fibrosis based on the Central Review Network (CRN) criteria. These scores are crucial for assessing the severity of liver disease and guiding treatment decisions."},
{"crn_fibrosis_scores__were_produced_by__mapping_gnn_derived_ordinal_grades_stages_to_bins": "The phrase \"were produced by\" indicates the method or process through which the CRN fibrosis scores were generated. In this context, it suggests that the scores were derived using a specific technique or algorithm."},
