{"incidence_trends_of_liver_cirrhosis_caused_by_nonalcoholic_steatohepatitis": "The incidence trends of liver cirrhosis caused by nonalcoholic steatohepatitis refer to the changing rates at which liver cirrhosis, a severe liver condition, occurs due to NASH over a period of time. This object of study is crucial for understanding the progression and impact of NASH on public health."},
{"zhai_m_et_al__published_in__sci_rep": "The predicate \"published in\" indicates that the research conducted by Zhai, M. et al. was submitted, reviewed, and accepted for publication in the scientific journal Sci. Rep., thereby making the findings accessible to the scientific community."},
{"sci_rep": "Sci. Rep., short for Scientific Reports, is a peer-reviewed, open-access scientific journal that publishes original research across all areas of the natural sciences. It is part of the Nature Portfolio and aims to provide a platform for high-quality research that may not fit within the scope of more specialized journals."},
