{"loomba_r_et_al__discussed__expert_panel_review_to_compare_fda_and_ema_guidance_on_drug_development_and_endpoints_in_nonalcoholic_steatohepatitis": "The predicate 'discussed' indicates that the subject, Loomba, R. et al., engaged in a detailed examination or analysis of a specific topic. In this context, it means that the authors reviewed and analyzed the differences and similarities between FDA and EMA guidance on drug development and endpoints in nonalcoholic steatohepatitis."},
{"expert_panel_review_to_compare_fda_and_ema_guidance_on_drug_development_and_endpoints_in_nonalcoholic_steatohepatitis": "The object 'Expert panel review to compare FDA and EMA guidance on drug development and endpoints in nonalcoholic steatohepatitis' refers to a comprehensive review conducted by an expert panel. This review aimed to compare the guidelines and recommendations provided by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) and the European Medicines Agency (EMA) regarding the development of drugs and the establishment of endpoints for clinical trials in the treatment of nonalcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH)."},
{"bedossa_p_flip_pathology_consortium": "Bedossa, P. & FLIP Pathology Consortium refers to a collaborative group led by Pierre Bedossa, focusing on the pathology and evaluation of liver diseases, particularly nonalcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD).|Here is another description: Bedossa, P. & FLIP Pathology Consortium is a group of researchers led by Pierre Bedossa, focused on the pathology of liver diseases, particularly nonalcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD). They are known for their work in developing and evaluating scoring systems for liver biopsies."},
