{"cryptogenic_cirrhosis_and_the_natural_history_of_non_alcoholic_fatty_liver_disease": "Cryptogenic cirrhosis refers to cirrhosis of the liver where the cause is unknown, and it is often associated with non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD). The natural history of NAFLD involves the progression of the disease from simple fatty liver to more severe conditions like cirrhosis."},
{"sanyal_a_j_et_al": "Sanyal, A. J. et al. refers to a group of researchers led by Arun J. Sanyal who conducted a study. This group is recognized for their contributions to the field of hepatology, particularly in the study of liver diseases such as nonalcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH)."},
