{"niddk": "The National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK) is a component of the National Institutes of Health (NIH) that supports and conducts research on many of the most serious diseases affecting public health. NIDDK provides funding for various research projects, including those related to diabetes, digestive disorders, and kidney diseases, through grants like the ones awarded to R.L.|Here is another description: The National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK) is a U.S. government agency dedicated to conducting and supporting research on diabetes, digestive diseases, kidney diseases, and other related conditions."},
