{"extended_data_fig_1": "Extended Data Fig. 1 is a supplementary figure that provides additional information or details related to the main content of a scientific publication. It is typically used to present data, models, or processes that support the primary findings of the research."},
{"extended_data_fig_1__describes__aim_mash_cnn_and_gnn_model_training_and_predictions": "The predicate \"describes\" indicates that Extended Data Fig. 1 provides a detailed explanation or representation of the AIM-MASH CNN and GNN model training and predictions. It serves as a visual and informative tool to help readers understand the processes and outcomes associated with these models."},
{"aim_mash_cnn_and_gnn_model_training_and_predictions": "The AIM-MASH CNN and GNN model training and predictions refer to the processes and results of training convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and graph neural networks (GNNs) using the AIM-MASH framework. This framework is designed to address metabolic dysfunction-associated steatohepatitis (MASH), a liver condition, by leveraging advanced machine learning techniques to improve diagnosis, understanding, and potentially treatment strategies."},
{"cnn__stands_for__convolutional_neural_network": "The phrase \"stands for\" is used to indicate that CNN is an abbreviation or acronym. It serves as a linguistic tool to clarify that the term CNN is a shortened form of a longer, more descriptive name."},
{"convolutional_neural_network": "Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is a class of deep neural networks, most commonly applied to analyzing visual imagery. They are also known as shift invariant or space invariant artificial neural networks (SIANN), based on their shared-weights architecture and translation invariance characteristics."},
{"gnn__stands_for__graph_neural_network": "The phrase \"stands for\" is used to indicate that GNN is an acronym or abbreviation that represents a longer, more descriptive term in the field of machine learning."},
{"graph_neural_network": "Graph neural network (GNN) is a type of neural network architecture that is specifically designed to process data represented in a graph format, where nodes can represent entities and edges the relationships between them."},
{"aim": "AIM is an acronym used in the context of machine learning models, specifically referring to a methodology or framework within the field."},
{"aim__stands_for__intelligence_based_measurement": "'Stands for' indicates that AIM is an abbreviation or shorthand notation representing a longer phrase or term in the context of machine learning and data analysis."},
{"intelligence_based_measurement": "Intelligence based Measurement is the full term that the acronym AIM represents, suggesting a method or approach that integrates intelligence, likely artificial intelligence, into the process of measurement or analysis."},
{"mash__stands_for__metabolic_dysfunction_associated_steatohepatitis": "The phrase \"stands for\" is used to indicate that MASH is an abbreviation or acronym representing a longer, more descriptive term. This helps in simplifying communication within the field by using a shorter form to refer to a complex condition."},
{"metabolic_dysfunction_associated_steatohepatitis": "Metabolic dysfunction-associated steatohepatitis is a medical condition characterized by inflammation of the liver, often associated with metabolic disorders. It is the full term that the acronym MASH represents, highlighting the condition's link to metabolic dysfunction."},
{"extended_data_fig_2": "Extended Data Fig. 2 is a supplementary figure that provides additional information or details related to the main content of a scientific publication. It is specifically designed to offer a visual representation of certain data or processes discussed in the text."},
